PdfCraft is an open source PDF workbench, a clean-room reimplementation of
the Adobe Acrobat workflow written in pure Rust by the ArtCraft team.  It
reads and renders PDFs, adds threaded comments and markup, fills in and
creates forms, signs and verifies documents, organizes, combines, splits
and edits pages, redacts content, protects files with passwords and
permissions, recognizes text in scanned pages (OCR) and exports PDFs to
other formats.

The pdfcraft-cli tool inspects, renders and checks PDFs from scripts and
runs the same engine commands, optionally as an MCP server for agents.
